-- title:
--   Strong approximation for norm-one units, indefinite rational case
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ with $0<a$ or $0<b$, and let $B=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra, assumed to be a division algebra in the sense that every nonzero $x\in B$ is a unit. Let $O\subseteq B$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is an order, i.e. $1\in O$, $O$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb Q$-span of $O$ is all of $B$, and $O$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb Z$. Let $y$ be a unit of $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$, where $\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb Q$, and assume: for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ and every ring isomorphism $\varphi$ from $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ onto $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q_w,a,b]$ (parameters taken along $\mathbb Q\to\mathbb Q_w$) which on pure tensors satisfies $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot z$ coordinatewise, the reduced norm $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a\,x_{i}^2-b\,x_{j}^2+ab\,x_{k}^2$ of $\varphi$ applied to the image of $y$ under localisation at $w$ equals $1$. Then there are $\beta\in B^{\times}$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\beta)=1$ and a unit $u$ of $B\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ stabilising, under multiplication, the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in O$ and $\alpha$ an adele integral at every place, such that $y$ equals the diagonal image of $\beta$ times $u$.
--
--   This is strong approximation for the norm-one group of an indefinite rational quaternion division algebra, in double-coset form: $B^{1}(\mathbb A^{f}_{\mathbb Q})=B^{1}(\mathbb Q)\cdot\widehat O^{1}$, the archimedean place serving as the non-compact place so that no finite place has to be left free. It is used in the treatment of maximal and Eichler orders, for instance to produce units of prescribed reduced norm and to compare adelic translates of orders.
-- source:
